# {{ site.title }}

> {{ site.description | safe }}

Andean Road is a personal travel guide to Chile written by one author — Karol, born in Chile, raised in New York. It is written in English, and every place listed here has been visited by the author personally; nothing is aggregated or scraped. Guides are multi-day itineraries, places are individual spots worth the trip, and practical pages cover the unglamorous essentials.

## The Atelier

The Map Atelier is a free browser-based map editor — pin places, apply a palette
and patterns, and share the finished map as a self-contained link. No account,
no upload, nothing installed.

- [The Atelier]({{ site.url }}/atelier/): what the editor makes and who it is for
- [Open the editor]({{ site.url }}/atelier/editor/): the editor itself

## Tools

Small single-purpose tools, free and entirely client-side.

- [Tools]({{ site.url }}/tools/): index of every public tool
- [Color Scales]({{ site.url }}/tools/color-scales/): blend two brand colors into a legible 5–11 step data-visualization scale; exports CSS, Figma tokens, SVG, PNG
- [Chromatlas]({{ site.url }}/tools/chromatlas/): Pantone's Colours of the Year as a browsable atlas, plus a harmony engine for any hue
- [SVG Map Editor]({{ site.url }}/tools/svg-editor/): recolor an SVG map by fill and stroke group, toggle layers, export — the file never leaves the browser
- [Internet Loom]({{ site.url }}/tools/internet-loom/): draft a weave on a grid loom from twill or huckaback; exports SVG or PNG

